  {
   "id": 99,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1520,
    470
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 11,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub director\n\n1. **Queue once** (Ctrl Enter). The scene render needs Blender (a few seconds), then the\n   director gets its previews.\n2. Click **open director** on the director node. Try:\n   - **+ layer → import image** (or drop / paste an image onto the canvas), move / scale / rotate it\n   - drag layers in the list: above **base** = in front of the facade, below = behind it\n   - select the base and set **holes** to e.g. `tag:ground_floor group:windows` (the arcade),\n     then a layer below the base shows only through those openings\n   - **mask by** another layer (shape / brightness, cut out), **clip to** a region (tool R)\n   - **+ layer → colour grade** or **paint layer**, blend modes, **?** for all shortcuts\n3. **apply** saves the composition into the node and queues again: composition, changed mask\n   and plan rules update. The plan node already reads the director's rules and regions; connect\n   a Region Sampler to it for the diffusion pass.\n\n**Light** (left, bottom): kubakub scene relight renders the model in Blender Cycles with the night\nHDRI, two warm area lights and the arcade glass glowing (regions mask on the ground floor windows). Its\nimage is the director's base. Lights are one per line in metres from the frame centre, the ground\nand the wall; environments: night, city, courtyard, sunset, sunrise, forest, studio, interior or a\nfile. Any mask (e.g. the director's layer masks) can feed emission_masks.\n\nSet the path of your scene file on node 1 (.fbx / .blend / .glb / .usd).\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
 ],
